attribute_on_document_root	<robot a="1" name="probe"><link name="l"></link></robot>	REFUSED xacro_structural_error	upstream sets an xacro:attribute on the element its input parent is, so as a child of the document's root the attribute lands on the root, while here xacro:attribute is not implemented yet and refuses as an unknown element
element_renamed_to_conditional	<robot name="probe"><link name="t"></link></robot>	REFUSED xacro_structural_error	upstream renames the node an xacro:element names and dispatches it again, so a name in xacro's namespace makes it the construct of that name, here a conditional, while here xacro:element is not implemented yet and refuses as an unknown element
element_renamed_to_macro_call	<robot name="probe"><link name="m"></link></robot>	REFUSED xacro_structural_error	upstream renames the node an xacro:element names and dispatches it again, so a macro's name in xacro's namespace makes it a call of that macro, while here xacro:element is not implemented yet and refuses as an unknown element
namespace_property_sees_later_global	<robot name="probe"><link name="alate"></link></robot>	REFUSED unsupported_expression	upstream evaluates a namespaced property in the namespace's table, whose parent is the including document's, at its first read, so it sees a global property bound after the include, while here the namespace is not implemented yet and the dotted name refuses as an unsupported call target
namespace_falls_through_to_parent	<robot name="probe"><link name="px"></link></robot>	REFUSED unsupported_expression	upstream reads a name a namespace lacks through the namespace's parent table, so a dotted read of a global property through the namespace renders it, while here the namespace is ignored and the dotted read refuses because no evaluator binds the namespace's name
namespace_parent_scope_skips_namespace	<robot name="probe"><link name="aS"></link><link name="aS"></link></robot>	REFUSED xacro_structural_error	upstream binds a parent-scoped property inside a namespaced macro in the caller's table, skipping the namespace table, so both the bare and the dotted read see it, while here the namespace is ignored and the dotted macro call refuses as an unknown element
namespace_replaced_by_second_include	REFUSED undefined_property	REFUSED unsupported_expression	upstream replaces a namespace when a second include binds the same name, so the first file's property is undefined through it, while here the namespace is ignored and the dotted read refuses because no evaluator binds the namespace's name
comment_evaluated_under_eval_comments	<robot name="probe"><link name="l"></link></robot> comments: <!-- v -->	<robot name="probe"><link name="l"></link></robot> comments:	upstream drops a comment holding xacro:eval-comments and evaluates each comment after it until an element, non-empty text or the off marker, while here comments are not parsed, so none reaches the expansion
comment_before_xacro_element_removed	<robot name="probe"><link name="l"></link></robot> comments: <!-- b -->	<robot name="probe"><link name="l"></link></robot> comments:	upstream deletes the comments directly before an element of xacro's grammar and keeps those before any other element, while here comments are not parsed, so none reaches the expansion
processing_instruction_kept	<robot name="probe"><link name="l"></link></robot> comments: <?probe value?>	<robot name="probe"><link name="l"></link></robot> comments:	upstream carries every processing instruction of the document into its output, while here processing instructions are not parsed, so none reaches the expansion
include_glob_matching_nothing	<robot name="probe"><link name="l"></link></robot>	REFUSED unresolved_include	upstream expands an include filename holding a glob character, warns when the pattern matches no file and includes nothing, so the rest of the document renders, while here include filenames are not globbed and the pattern is looked for as a file of that name, which refuses where none is
include_namespace_not_text	REFUSED xacro_structural_error	<robot name="probe"><link name="i"></link></robot>	upstream evaluates an include's namespace and keys a table by it, so a namespace whose value is a list, which cannot key a table, refuses there, while here the namespace attribute is not implemented yet and the include reads into the including scope
property_removes_builtin	<robot name="probe"><link name="l3.141592653589793"></link></robot>	<robot name="probe"><link name="l"></link></robot>	upstream keeps a built-in constant that a property removes, warning that it cannot be removed, while here the removal binds the name empty
comment_evaluation_switched_off	<robot name="probe"><link name="l"></link></robot> comments: <!-- v --> <!-- ${x} -->	<robot name="probe"><link name="l"></link></robot> comments:	upstream evaluates each comment after one holding xacro:eval-comments and stops at one holding xacro:eval-comments:off, keeping the later comment verbatim, while here no comment is kept
find_without_package_index	REFUSED unknown_substitution	REFUSED unresolved_find	upstream reads a find through a package index the pinned install does not ship, so without one every find refuses as an unsupported substitution, while here a find no configured source answers refuses as unresolved
